    },
    "message": "Check the resource ledger's current state instead of replaying it\n\nEvery inventory operation deep-copied the whole ledger and replayed the\nfull audit trail before and after the change, and the per-tick world\nvalidation and metric capture replayed it again every minute. The audit\ntrail has no limit, so the cost grew with Run length; the replay also\nchecked reservation reuse against a list.\n\nOperations, per-tick validation and metric capture now use\nvalidate_resource_ledger_state: current balances, active reservations,\nthe audit records from the last tick, and each resource's newest audit\nrecord against its account. An operation works on a candidate with\ncopied accounts and lists and commits only after that check.\nvalidate_resource_ledger still replays the whole trail at Run start and\nend and at Checkpoint capture and restore, now with a set for reuse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UATazG2GqTVweGMJTJEbNT",
